SQL [till2]> select label, ok, detail from _till_proof order by n
  ✓ T1 · a reversal without a pointer, a charge WITH one, a free-text reason and an unknown kind are refused (23514); a second reversal of the same payment is refused (23505); a proper reversal goes in
  ✓ T2 · undo Mark paid: the charge row is KEPT, one reversal row points at it, nothing is deleted or logged as a would-be delete; the netted status is 'unpaid'; the chain holds both payment entries, the reversal with its pointer and reason
  ✓ T3 · undo collected: one reversal (reason undo_collected), the charge kept, status 'unpaid', the order back to accepted as v3 (state_change) — and no deletion entry
  ✓ T9 · the actor's ROLE: till_record_actor names exactly the two entries the undo made (the reversal and order v3) as 'staff'; a second call changes nothing (first role kept); no name or id is stored
  ✓ T9b · a role outside owner / staff / admin / system / unknown, or an action that is not a short word, is refused (23514) — a name cannot get in
  ✓ T4 · failed refund: 'refunded' before, then the refund is reversed (reason refund_failed) — the refund row kept, the order 'paid:500' again, nothing deleted
  ✓ T5 · collect → undo → collect again: today's key collides (23505 — why ledger.ts suffixes it after a reversal), the suffixed key goes in, and the order reads paid once
  ✓ T6 · counter refund (cash, 4.00 of 10.00): one refund row, channel in_person_other, method cash, reason item_unavailable — chained with them; the order 'paid:600'
  ✓ T7 · Q5: the cancelled counter-paid order gets one refund row (card, 5.00, reason order_cancelled); the order is 'refunded' and its v2 is the cancellation (state_change)
  ✓ T8 · an offline walk-up's device evidence is stored BEFORE its order, so v1 carries it ({device_id, fingerprint, created_at}) and till_id is the device id; a second call for the same order — or for an order that already exists (an older app's sync) — stores nothing; an order without it seals as before (till_id manual, no device key)
  ✓ T8b · a truck outside the till (a demo truck, the default) stores no device row
  ✓ T10 · a code rollback's old undo (DELETE of a reversed charge) is not blocked: its reversal goes with it (cascade), both deletions chained, till_verify true
  ✓ T11 · till_device_fingerprints and till_entry_actors refuse UPDATE / DELETE (HGT01)
  ✓ T12 · an order with no device row seals exactly till-pack-1b's 37 keys; a payment with no pointer and no reason exactly the 12 — so no entry written before this migration stops matching
  ✓ T13 · till_verify(truck A) at the end: ok — chain, identity references, versions, deltas, till_id, VAT reconciliation; every row matches its sealed form
  ✓ T14 · after every step, every order and payment row of both trucks carries this transaction's own xid — no till trigger wrote one
